  "name": "The_Prestige",
  "description": "The Prestige: Benchmarking Cognitive Visual Reasoning using Magic Tricks (NeurIPS 2026, Track on Evaluations and Datasets). The Prestige is a video question-answering benchmark built from professional magic performances. Magicians deliberately misdirect their audience, so the questions take more than object recognition. A model has to track objects through a long routine, remember what was shown earlier, explain why a reveal surprises the audience, and reject questions that rest on false premises. The benchmark has 2,177 open-ended questions in six categories. Each question is anchored to a timestamp in a YouTube video and has a human-written reference answer. The videos are referenced by YouTube ID, belong to their creators, and are not redistributed. Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.38103. Website: https://stevvwen.github.io/prestige-website/. Code: https://github.com/stevvwen/The_prestige.",
  "alternateName": [
    "SediRockStar/The_Prestige",
    "The Prestige"
  ],
